  "id": "v04_increase_second_mandate",
  "title": "An increase covered by a second mandate verifies",
  "test_plan_vector": "4",
  "spec": [
    "Platform Verification 4: MUST evaluate `seq` and `prev` continuity per `(iss, mandate_ref)` chain. A second, different receipt for a `seq` the platform already holds is `receipt_sequence_gap`; the platform keeps both.",
    "Platform Verification 6: MUST check, on the recomputed totals, that `authorized` and `captured` do not exceed `mandated` (`receipt_exceeds_mandate`) and that `refunded` does not exceed `captured` (`receipt_refund_exceeds_capture`).",
    "Business Requirements 3: MUST NOT authorize or capture so that `authorized` or `captured` exceeds `mandated`. Any increase in what the buyer pays beyond `mandated` (a tip, an overage, an order change, or a re-authorization above the original amount) MUST be covered by a new closed Payment Mandate from the platform. Movements that spend against the new mandate form their own chain, keyed by its `mandate_ref`."
  ],
